<title>USA: FORECAST-US inflation tame, jobs fewer into 1998.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-US inflation tame, jobs fewer into 1998.</headline>
<byline>Jeff Coelho</byline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Economists read the tea leaves last week and saw a U.S. economy for the next two years with creeping inflation growth and some labor market weakness.</p>
<p>They said the recent runup in energy prices will inevitably seep into other consumer sectors and demand for higher wages will eventually choke profit margins. But they said the process would be gradual and somewhat deceiving.</p>
</text>
